    "bitcoin_integration": "Neutral-to-permissive but no bespoke crypto law. Barbados has no specific Bitcoin/crypto licensing statute; crypto is not banned and operates in a guidance/sandbox environment. The Central Bank of Barbados and Financial Services Commission ran a Regulatory Sandbox (Bitt was the first entrant to exit) and Barbados piloted a central-bank digital currency (DCash). No official statement designates Bitcoin as legal tender, and there is no dedicated crypto-asset regulatory framework equivalent to the Bahamas' DARE Act or Cayman's VASP Act."
